Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — source-developed working scene
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-10-10
Status: Independent screenplay development under DEC-0019; refinements during production

INT. SECURE EVIDENCE OFFICE - TUESDAY MORNING

A table, a handover form, Ruth and an evidence officer. Elias waits out of the transaction. Zoe puts the envelope down first.

ZOE across the flap.

Ruth checks the unbroken seal.

RUTH
Separately with me. Under your instructions, subject to the legal limits we discussed.

ZOE
Not with the drive. If anything changes?

RUTH
I'll explain what changes and why, as far as I'm lawfully able.

A separate receipt goes to Zoe. The envelope moves into Ruth custody, not into the officer's evidence bag.

Zoe removes the archive hard drive from the backpack. Sets it on the table herself.

The officer checks the documented item, handling conditions and original-preservation record. Relevant access to restricted child information will be recorded. Previously preserved copies remain distinct.

EVIDENCE OFFICER
Read the form first. Ask before you sign.

Zoe reads it. Checks one item against Ruth explanation. The officer waits. No speech about being brave.

She signs. Her handwriting looks oddly small.

The officer bags the original, seals it and marks the time: 09:42. The custody reference goes on Zoe's receipt. The officer, not Zoe, is now responsible for its protected handling.

The scuffed black backpack lies flat on the table. Elias repaired strap is still visible. It is suddenly only a bag.

EVIDENCE OFFICER
Do you want that back?

ZOE
Yes.

She puts the receipts in her coat with the notebook. The backpack goes over one shoulder. Its familiar weight is absent.

At the door she looks back once. Ruth has the envelope. The officer has the sealed drive. Nobody has taken the notebook.

EXT. SECURE OFFICE - MORNING

Elias joins her outside.

He notices the backpack, then waits for Zoe to speak.

ZOE
It's light.

ELIAS
Yes.

For once there is no need to explain the obvious. They walk towards the car. Her next meeting is with her friend, not with another file.
